Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:01:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] Flash Next CUDA: NVFP4 experts on prompt tiles with the
 decode form's sums, bit for bit

A ModelOpt NVFP4 checkpoint's routed experts ran the decode kernel on prompt chunks: plans of
16 pairs an item, so a 1,536-row chunk read each expert's weights two to three times.

prompt_tiles gets a FACT flag: each 16-input block is one mma of the raw codes from zero, then
fma(p, its e4m3 scale, acc), blocks in ascending K, then the global scale and the epilogue, the
decode form's arithmetic in its order. Two entries, tf_nvfp4_fact_swiglu and
tf_nvfp4_fact_down_f32, on 64-pair plans (Nvfp4Experts.runFact); the ModelOpt expert path takes
them from 64 rows a pass (TF_FLASHNEXT_FACT_ROWS, 0 for never). Without the flag the template is
unchanged: the 55 existing nvfp4_experts functions' SASS equals main's on sm_80/86/89/120/121.

tf-cuda-test nvfp4-fact: bytes equal to the decode form at 1 to 300 rows, FP64-bounded, the
scaled-code prompt tile as a red control. Kernel contract: both entries replace the decode
instances (gate 3 bit-equal), gate 4 on integer sums, the scaled-code tile as a control red at
gate 3, gate 5 records from nvcc 13.0.88.

(cherry picked from commit 074e0ec378911a59072fcab8e273af44fca28405)
